<title>POLAND: Polish firms show Jan-Dec PLN 8.5 bln net profit.</title>
<headline>Polish firms show Jan-Dec PLN 8.5 bln net profit.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish enterprises reported an overall 8.5 billion zloty net profit in 1996 period, flat from 1995, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>GUS said the private sector had a net profit of 5.7 billion zlotys on total revenues of 270.9 billion in the period against a profit of 3.3 billion and sales of 180.6 billion in the same period last year.</p>
<p>The state-owned sector reported a profit of 2.8 billion on sales of 272.2 billion versus last year's 5.2 billion and 237.1 billion respectively.</p>
<p> POLISH ENTERPRISES RESULTS		 1996    1995</p>
<p> total revenues bln PLN		    543.1   417.8</p>
<p> total costs				   527.4   401.3</p>
<p> total net profit				8.5     8.5</p>
<p> total gross profit			   18.4    17.5</p>
<p> net profit margin (pct)		     1.6     2.0</p>
<p> gross profit margin (pct)		   3.4     4.2</p>
<p> liquidity ratio     (pct)		  22.2    22.7</p>
<p>NOTES: Data collected from all companies employing more than 50 people in main sectors of the economy.</p>
<p>Liquidity ratio is a percentage relation of cash reserves and tradable securities to short-term liabilities.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
